## 2. Voice and quality

- Output must read like a **real tenant submission**, not a spec or checklist.
- Use **natural, simple English (CEFR about B1–B2)** — clear words, short sentences, still professional enough for work orders.
- **Do not use placeholders** (no `TBD`, `[name]`, `XXX`, or “your city here”). Use **plausible fictional** names, numbers, and addresses instead.
- **Do not exaggerate** drama or add long backstory. Stick to what a resident would type.
- **Vary scenarios** across runs: plumbing, electrical, HVAC, appliances, structural, etc.
- Mix **emergency** and **non-emergency** examples when generating **multiple** work orders; for a **single** example, pick one level and stay consistent.
- **Emergency** examples should include **clear urgency signals** (active leak, gas/smoke smell, no heat when very cold, sparking, flooding, etc.) when appropriate.
- **Avoid repeating** the same opening lines, same address pattern, or same issue type across consecutive examples.

---

## 3. Structure (follow exactly)

Use this section order and headings. **Description** and **PM Note** follow the rules below.

```markdown
Title:
<short, clear issue title>

Client:
<realistic full name>

Creation Date (UTC):
<realistic datetime>

Location:
<real US or Canada address>

Phone:
<realistic phone number format>

Description:
- Write like a tenant (not technical).
- 3-5 bullet points describing symptoms.
- Include timing (when it started).
- Include observable facts only (no diagnosis unless obvious).

PM Note:
- Short, technical note for maintenance team.
- Mention likely cause and what to check.

Resident Availability:
<realistic schedule>

Image Descriptions:
- Provide 3 realistic photo descriptions (not URLs).
- Each should describe what the tenant would photograph.
```

### Field rules

| Section | Rules |
|--------|--------|
| **Title** | Short issue label a PM would scan (e.g. “Bathroom ceiling stain”, not a paragraph). |
| **Client** | Realistic full name (vary cultures; avoid famous names). |
| **Creation Date (UTC)** | Believable timestamp; can be recent. |
| **Location** | Realistic **US or Canada** street address (include unit/apt if typical). |
| **Phone** | Valid-looking format for that region (do not use real public hotlines as “the tenant’s” number). |
| **Description** | **Tenant voice** — bullets only under **Description**, 3–5 bullets, symptoms + when it started + what they see/hear/smell. No jargon like “compressor short cycle” unless the tenant would say it. |
| **PM Note** | **Internal / technical** — likely cause, parts to check, safety note if needed. Keep short. |
| **Resident Availability** | Concrete windows (weekdays, evenings, weekend) in plain language. |
| **Image Descriptions** | Exactly **three** lines (or three bullets), each describing a **photo the tenant would plausibly send** (wide shot, close-up, label, etc.). **No URLs.** These lines are the **brief** the agent uses for generated images (below). |

